US English speaker learning Cantonese (not Mandarin), A1, ordering at a Hong Kong cha chaan teng. Every Cantonese word and sentence is spoken Cantonese written in traditional characters, with Cantonese-only words where Cantonese uses them ("唔該", "係", "嘅", "咩", "喺", "幾多錢"), never Mandarin wording ("谢谢", "是", "的", "什么", "在", "多少钱") or simplified characters. Romanization is Jyutping with tone numbers ("m4 goi1"), never pinyin. Tips name Cantonese sounds and tones English speakers get wrong.